    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0793" n="1751" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1751"/>

                <head>No. 8.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 1, 1887</date>.
                        (Received February 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 12th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to inform you that under date of the 27th ultimo the
                    Marquis of Salisbury <pb facs="0794" n="1752" xml:id="pg1752"/> instructs me to
                    inquire whether the inform and papers reia tive to the seizure of the British
                    schooners <hi rendition="#italic">Carolena, Onward</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thornton</hi> have reached the United States
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
